			"Message": "build(deps): bump pnpm/action-setup from 6.0.3 to 6.0.4\n\nBumps [pnpm/action-setup](https://github.com/pnpm/action-setup) from 6.0.3 to 6.0.4.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/pnpm/action-setup/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/pnpm/action-setup/compare/v6.0.3...v6.0.4)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: pnpm/action-setup\n  dependency-version: 6.0.4\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>",
			"SHA": "e030ea5bb8011a0a2e194d62cf8837f61ec8569c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T20:26:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				106,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add window close handling, lifecycle focus, and command catalog smoke test\n\nAdd three related enhancements to Sky's bridge and entry point:\n\n1. **Window close handler** (`sky://window/close-requested`): When Mountain emits this (user hit Cmd+W or clicked window X), try to close the active editor first via `workbench.action.closeActiveEditor`. Only fall through to actually closing the window via `nativeHost:closeWindow` if no editor is open. This matches stock VS Code's Cmd+W behavior.\n\n2. **Lifecycle focus** (`sky://lifecycle/phaseChanged`): After window restoration (phase 3), force focus into the workbench DOM so the active Monaco editor becomes the keyboard target without requiring a click. Uses cascade of selectors to find the active textarea, then falls back to the workbench root, then the body.\n\n3. **Command catalog smoke test**: New opt-in harness (`?land-smoke=1` or `localStorage.LAND_SMOKE_TEST=1`) that validates every command in Wind's generated `CommandCatalog` is known to the workbench's command service. Reports summary to console and emits `cel:smoke-test:complete` event. Zero observable overhead when disabled.\n\nThe smoke test module is dynamically imported with `@vite-ignore` to avoid build-time resolution failures when Wind's codegen hasn't run yet.",
			"SHA": "1270c6090626f6ac658e20654ed32fc4c81e806e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Auto",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T02:37:12Z",
