			"SHA": "f49c6c8b1626d1711e28080587bd6147f8bf4ad5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-30T01:23:23Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				104,
				7
			],
			"Message": "build(Sky): Fix Bundled variant build by using dynamic imports and Vite stub plugin\n\nConvert static imports of Bundled/*/Layout.astro components to dynamic `await import()` in Astro frontmatter. The previous static imports forced Rollup to walk every variant's VS Code module graph, including Browser's `workbench.web.main.internal.js` which exists only in the gulp-only `out/` tree and carries unmangled symbol references that cannot resolve against Output's release `out-build/` tree (mangled, telemetry-stripped).\n\nAlso add the `BundledEntryStubInactive` Vite plugin in astro.config.ts that replaces inactive variant Entry.ts modules with an empty stub at `load()` time. This short-circuits Rollup's graph walk for variants not in the active `Pack` env var while leaving the active variant's Entry bundled normally through `BundledInputs`.\n\nThe `SkyChannels.ts` auto-generated file is also included, documenting all 59 `sky://` IPC channels Mountain can emit and whether Sky has listeners for each.",
			"SHA": "2d34bedf16b716c0f927c8a3b83faf9c4bbfe852"
		}
	],
